.TH "CHECK_CERT" "1" "April 2026" "NMS_Tools" "TLS Certificate Inspection Tool"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
\f[B]check_cert\f[R] \[em] TLS certificate inspection and policy
enforcement tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]check_cert\f[R] -H [-p ] options
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]check_cert\f[R] performs deterministic TLS certificate inspection,
extracting metadata, validating chains, enforcing hostname rules, and
evaluating OCSP and algorithm strength policies.
.PP
It is suitable for: - Monitoring certificate expiration
.PD 0
.P
.PD
- Enforcing TLS policy
.PD 0
.P
.PD
- Detecting misconfigurations
.PD 0
.P
.PD
- Automation pipelines
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Target
.PP
\f[B]-H, \[en]host \f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Target hostname.
.PP
\f[B]-p, \[en]port \f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
TLS port (default: 443).
.SS Validation
.PP
\f[B]\[en]require-hostname-match\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Fail if certificate CN/SAN does not match host.
.PP
\f[B]\[en]require-ocsp-good\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Require OCSP status \f[V]good\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]\[en]require-tls13-only\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Fail if TLS < 1.3 is negotiated.
.SS Metadata Extraction
.PP
Extracts: - Expiration
